@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Output readability — sbx's principles in proveo's own idiom, across every command
' purpose: the delivery plan for making proveo's stream read like sbx's, without copying sbx's look
'   the vocabulary it amends ....... _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml
'   the design language ............ _spec/_conventions/tui-design-language.puml
'   the step lines ................. _spec/internal/ui/step-lines.puml
'   the design and its critique .... scratchpad of session e2da2921 (2026-11-11), summarised here
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS MEASURED (2026-11-11) ─────────────────────────────────────────
' One `proveo run claudecode` on a linked-worktree monorepo put 58 proveo rows
' on screen before the agent started; the longest was 235 columns. Workspace
' facts appeared in five places, and sbx's own create block then listed the
' mounts again. Sections were named by phase ("execution", "starting"), so
' "interface" printed between step 2/5 and step 4/5. Every fact carried a ●
' and most lines carried their own reason in parentheses.
' sbx's create block, in the same terminal, read better: sections named by
' subject, one item per line with a short result after " — ", aligned
' key/value blocks, detail dim on the next line, home-relative paths, and one
' closing outcome line.
'
' ── WHAT THE OPERATOR DECIDED (2026-11-11) ─────────────────────────────────
'   "adopt the principles, but don't copy the design verbatim"
'   scope ........ every command (run, init, adopt, attach/schedule, clean,
'                  ls/projects, rm, setup, uninstall, update)
'   sbx overlap .. proveo says only what sbx cannot: what sbx's create block
'                  prints (mounts, kit, image, CPU, memory, port publishing)
'                  leaves proveo's screen and stays in the run log; a
'                  re-attach, which has no sbx block, prints it. The image
'                  was a wrong premise; see decision D below
'   IDE attach ... one row on a live run; the JetBrains, Toolbox and VS Code
'                  text goes to the run log; a kept sandbox still prints all
'   fact rows .... keep the ● role dots and colours; align "key: value" in
'                  one column per block; detail dim under the value
' NOT CHOSEN: sbx's Title-case "Key:" column (the operator: not verbatim);
' capturing sbx's block (a hidden sbx prompt would hang); keeping both voices.
' proveo-dev is the maintainer CLI behind mise tasks and is out of scope
' unless the operator asks.
'
' ── THE RULES (sbx's principle → proveo's rule) ────────────────────────────
'   P1 subject  A heading names the subject its lines describe, in one
'               lowercase word. sbx's own block runs under "sbx".
'   P2 item     A state is one line: mark, item, " — ", a short result.
'   P3 facts    Facts about one subject print as ONE ui.Facts block: role
'               dot, "key:", value; values start in one column per block;
'               a list value stacks under the value column.
'   P4 detail   Secondary detail goes on its own dim line, under the value
'               (a fact) or two columns past the text (an item). Never a
'               parenthetical sentence, never a second " — " clause.
'   P5 paths    Host paths on screen go through ui.Tilde. Guest paths,
'               every --print line and the log-only blocks stay absolute.
'               Mode flags trail in parentheses: (rw), (ro), (copy).
'   P6 what     A screen line says what a thing is or what happened. The
'               why goes to _spec, the how-to-change to the flag's help,
'               maintainer commands to the run log.
'   P7 outcome  A block ends on a ✓/⚠/× line only when it reaches a verdict
'               its facts do not already state: workspace ends on ✓ private
'               clone or ✓ mounted checkout; credentials ends on its ⚠/×
'               when one exists; run and egress stay facts only. Follow-ups
'               go dim under that line. (Amended 2026-11-11, decision A; it
'               read "a block ends on its outcome line".)
'   P8 marks    ✓ done · ⚠ attention · × failed · ● a role-coloured fact or a
'               running step (the operator kept the dots on facts).
'   P9 once     Each fact is said once per run, on screen or in sbx's block;
'               the run log keeps the full record. sbx's block names only
'               the kit-built image tag, so proveo's image is proveo's to
'               say (decision D).
'
' ── THE OPERATOR'S DECISIONS ON R1'S OPEN FORKS (2026-11-11) ──────────────
'   A result lines  A block ends on a ✓/⚠/× line only for a verdict its
'                   facts do not state (P7 above). NOT CHOSEN: an outcome
'                   line on every block; a credentials ✓ line in place of
'                   the login fact.
'   B host add-ons  Android emulator, host Chrome over CDP, Hermes Desktop:
'                   the "<add-on> — starting" live line leaves the screen
'                   once the add-on is up; each add-on is then ONE aligned
'                   fact in the interface block ("android: emulator-5554
'                   (AVD Pixel_9)", "chrome: …", "desktop: …"); progress
'                   lines and the Desktop install plan go to the run log;
'                   warnings stay ⚠ interface items. NOT CHOSEN: an egress
'                   fact; a new "host" heading.
'   C log paths     The run log's header records "home: <absolute $HOME>"
'                   once, so each teed "~/" resolves; rows stay as drawn.
'                   NOT CHOSEN: "~/" unexplained; a tee that writes
'                   absolute paths.
'   D image row     MEASURED (R1 round-2 review, sbx v0.50.0, a sandbox made
'                   for it): sbx's SANDBOX block reads "Image:
'                   sbx-kit-src:proveo-claudecode-0148841a44ae", the tag its
'                   kit build makes, and never names proveo's image. So a
'                   create run's sbx block prints ONE fact right before "●
'                   sbx create": "image: proveo/claudecode-browser:latest
'                   (published)" or "… (local build)" (posture.Image: the
'                   :local tag is the local build). A re-attach keeps its
'                   image fact from the receipt. NOT CHOSEN: the image only
'                   when non-default; the image in the run log only.
'
' ── TECHNICAL CALLS (the Executor's, from the design review) ──────────────
'   One shared helper, ui.Facts, aligns by display width, wraps a value at
'   its own column on the terminal only (the log copy stays unwrapped), and
'   prints aligned plain text in plain mode.
'   Lines that stay on screen drop "step n/N ·"; live frames and the run log
'   keep the numbers.
'   Each subject prints once, after the step that makes it true: the
'   workspace block after the mount plan, the interface block after sbx
'   create.
'
' ── WAVES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   R0  internal/ui: Fact, Facts, Detailf, Tilde, SectionSbx, the hanging
'       wrap; output-vocabulary.puml; unit tests. No caller changes.
'   R1  the start of `proveo run`, up to "● <agent> — starting"
'       (internal/run, internal/backend/sandbox): sections by subject, fact
'       blocks, the sbx overlap rule, the one-row IDE line, step lines.
'   R2  the end of a run: results, teardown, kept sandboxes, adopt/review
'       hints (teardown.go, results.go, pushed.go, sandbox.go's results).
'   R3  `proveo init`: the apply stream, the result block, the verify step.
'   R4  the other commands: adopt, attach and schedule, clean, ls and
'       projects, rm, setup, uninstall, update, version.
' Each wave: lint, both builds, the unit baseline, the named e2e tests whose
' anchors it moves (macOS; linux/arm64 where they run), the specs it touches,
' and this file's PROGRESS.
'
' ── E2E ANCHORS THAT MOVE (R1) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
'   e2e/instrument_test.go:61 "run log: (\S+\.log)" — and it must expand "~/"
'     (a failed read returns "" silently)
'   e2e/browser_viewport_test.go:85 "browser viewport: (http://\S+)", now
'     read from the run log; the screen row reads "browser: the agent's
'     Chromium over CDP"
'   e2e/project_env_test.go:25 "project .env: 1 value(s) seeded into"
'   e2e/clone_output_test.go:69,72 and e2e/sbx_test.go:623 "backend: docker
'     sandboxes (sbx)", "lifts it back here at teardown"
'   e2e/ide_attach_test.go:76-82 the JetBrains, VS Code and "a local Open"
'     strings, which move to the run log
'   e2e/idle_test.go:69-89 the "agent: <target> " filter; its runIDPattern
'     read the run ID in the log row as a sandbox name (sandboxNameIn now)
'   e2e/sbx_egress_test.go:61 "allows every host" under --print
'   e2e/stream_palette_test.go: whiteRun and the sbx-block boundary
'   e2e/ports_publish_test.go:95,134 "→ sandbox :<port>" (found while moving
'     the list above; the screen row reads "port <n>: <what it serves>", and
'     the test reads the host port from the run log's "port <n>: http://…")
'   e2e/opencode_engine_sbx_test.go:219,280,292 "re-attaching to <engine>,"
'   e2e/credentials_test.go secretLineNamesAny (stale since sbx's OAuth slots
'     kept claudecode's keys out of the "secret store first:" line)
'   e2e/android_addon_test.go:65 "android: booting AVD" + "booted" (round 3,
'     decision B): now read from the run log; the pane must hold the fact
'     "android: emulator-<n> (AVD …" and not the boot progress
'   e2e/host_adb_sbx_test.go hostadb.Ensure's new (Started, error) return
'
' ── PROGRESS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   R0 ... done 2026-11-11: ui.Fact/Facts, Detailf, Tilde (schedule's
'          tildeHome removed), the hanging wrap (wrapWriter.writeHang, multi
'          forwards it to the terminal half), output-vocabulary.puml FACTS
'          AND DETAIL. No caller prints a Facts block yet. SectionSbx moves
'          to R1: the contract test needs a caller for every Section*.
'   R1 ... done 2026-11-11, uncommitted, fixed after two reviews. Headings
'          up to the agent's start, each drawn once in a run:
'          run · credentials · egress · workspace · sbx · interface.
'          run      the log row after the pages, the scope folded in (the
'                   scope heading prints only in the numbered picker); a run
'                   that fails before it still prints the log row, under
'                   "run", before any held item (run.endEarly); the image
'                   pull, before credentials; an sbx install or upgrade, the
'                   one line before the log row ("sbx — installing" or "sbx —
'                   upgrading", the command dim)
'          credentials  ONE block (resolveCredentials → PrintBlock): login
'                   (store role, "none found" or "persisted in the proveo
'                   home"), "env token: <VAR> set, not injected", withheld;
'                   then ⚠ refresh, gaps, role keys, unknown model ids
'          egress   ONE block: sbx's baseline as a cloud-role "network" fact
'                   and the local model, printed after the model is served;
'                   the auto pick's reason and opt-out go to the run log
'          workspace  sandbox.ReportWorkspace after Spec: checkout (worktree
'                   only), .env (the clone's copy), output, links (file
'                   targets sbx never binds are ⚠ items with no reason on
'                   screen), ⚠ items with every home path as "~/" (TildeIn),
'                   then the ✓ outcome; --print leads with "proveo home"
'          sbx      Spec's notes, the live steps, the stale Hand when a stale
'                   sandbox exists (retire lines unnumbered), then ONE Facts
'                   block: a "secret" row per stored secret, the env-file
'                   seed, proveo's image last; "● sbx create" and sbx's
'                   block; a re-attach prints the secrets and the kept
'                   sandbox's own record (image, kit dir, cpus, memory from
'                   the receipt; mounts from sbx's row) as that block and
'                   flags a workspace block it cannot vouch for
'          interface  after sbx create, only when it has a row: what each
'                   port serves (a stopped kept sandbox's host ports come
'                   from its receipt), the browser row, one fact per host
'                   add-on (chrome, android, desktop), the "android app"
'                   rows, the ⚠ reach items, forgotten ports and apps, one
'                   "ide" row
'          start    "● <target> <version> — starting"
'          Log-only: backend, variant, the local-build note, agent pin + mise
'          hint, proveo home line, gh line, the create block's facts, the IDE
'          block, port URLs and commands, the CDP how-to, the reasons the
'          screen dropped, the host add-ons' progress, the Desktop install
'          plan, the auto local model's reason, each Item.Log line, the
'          home the "~/" rows resolve to. Lines that stay drop "step n/N"; the log keeps
'          each place, under its heading (Steps.do draws it first).
'          A failure before a block prints still prints its ⚠ items
'          (run.reportUnhanded, sandbox.Run's deferred flush).
'          FOUND: the gh line was false; proveo's WorkspaceBinds drops the
'          bind (credential-boundary.puml, a bug to fix separately).
'          FOUND (review): a symlink to a FILE was named in the links fact,
'          but sbx binds directories only (mount-symlink-escape.puml).
'          MEASURED (review, sbx v0.50.0, a sandbox made for it and removed):
'          sbx's create block prints "✓ port 8080/tcp4 — published
'          127.0.0.1:47123" (P9 holds; the browser row lost its ":9222"
'          detail); a stopped sandbox lists no ports and gets the same host
'          port back on `sbx run` (kit-lifecycle.puml).
'          LOST: the measured run's log (proveo-1794413821-11931.log). keep=20
'          pruned it while e2e runs wrote into ~/.proveo/logs. The trace ran
'          against readability_0's BEFORE list instead; every fact lands on
'          screen or in ui.Logf. A wave copies its measured log first.
'          e2e: idle_test reads the sandbox name, not the run ID, from the
'          screen (it failed at HEAD too). Passed after the review on macOS:
'          clone_output, ide_attach, project_env, both android, browser
'          viewport, ports publish, stream palette, idle (45s), the --print
'          set. Skipped here: the OpenCode engine (no proveo/opencode image)
'          and docker access (no harness credential env).
'          RE-ATTACH, exercised by hand (a sandbox made for it, removed): a
'          killed run left proveo-claudecode-<hash>; the next run printed
'          image, kit, mounts under "sbx", then "● re-attach to <name> — left
'          by an earlier run", "ide" alone under "interface". cpus and memory
'          print only when proveo set them; sbx's own default leaves the
'          receipt empty.
'          DECIDED (the operator, 2026-11-11) AND BUILT IN ROUND 3: A, B, C and
'          D above. A: P7 amended; the code already ended workspace on its ✓,
'          credentials on its items (sandbox.PrintBlock), run and egress on
'          facts. B: hostadb.Ensure → Started, hostcdp.Ensure → Opened,
'          Deps.EnsureDesktop → (launch, installed, err); run.startAddon logs
'          every report and, in plain output, its start line; Input and Spec
'          carry InterfaceFacts. C: runlog.Open writes "home: <$HOME>".
'          D: report.imageFact via posture.Image, last in the sbx block.
'          ROUND 3 FIXES (the round-2 review): the auto local model's line
'          went to the run log (one screen line: egress's fact); endEarly
'          prints the log row under "run" before the held items, pinned
'          through Do's own defers; the remembered port/app warnings stay
'          after the form: MEASURED, the form draws on the alternate screen
'          (dev-ports.puml); secrets, env seed and image are one Facts block;
'          Item.Log carries the why and how-to (re-attach's plan note, the
'          buildx knob, sbx secret set); "sbx — upgrading"; settings errors
'          and the retire's lift line go through ui.TildeIn/Tilde (the lift
'          line is teardown's too, so R2 inherits it); sbx reports no
'          sandbox CPU or memory, so a re-attach prints them only when proveo
'          set them (MEASURED, kit-lifecycle.puml); the stale spec text on
'          the idle name and on unknownModel; the receipt comment's history
'          clause; --print e2e runs under a t.TempDir() PROVEO_HOME
'          (testing-strategy.puml; the idle test keeps the real one).
'          KNOWN, NOT FIXED: the workspace ✓ prints before the stale step
'          decides which sandbox runs (report.go ReportWorkspace); a ⚠ under
'          "sbx" corrects it for a kept sandbox, as at HEAD. The OpenCode
'          engine and docker-access e2e skip for a missing image or harness
'          credential. The measured run's log stays LOST. An OpenCode engine
'          created in the stale path prints its sbx facts after sbx's block
'          (ensureOpenCodeEngine runs `sbx create` itself).
'   R2 ... not started
'   R3 ... not started
'   R4 ... not started

component "sbx's create block\nsubject sections · items · aligned facts" as SBX <<cloud>>
component "proveo's stream, 2026-11-11\nphase sections · prose · ● on every line" as OLD <<error>>
component "the rules P1–P9\nin proveo's idiom" as RULES <<app>>
component "ui.Facts · Detailf · Tilde\nR0" as UI <<app>>
component "run start · run end · init · the rest\nR1 · R2 · R3 · R4" as WAVES <<app>>
component "the run log\nthe full record" as LOG <<data>>

SBX ARROW_MAIN RULES : the principles, not the look
OLD ARROW_ERROR RULES : what they fix
RULES ARROW_MAIN UI
UI ARROW_MAIN WAVES
WAVES ARROW_OPTIONAL LOG : what leaves the screen

note bottom of RULES
  **Principles, not the look.** proveo keeps its
  rules, its lowercase keys and its ● dots. It
  takes sbx's subject sections, aligned facts,
  dim detail and one-line outcomes.
end note

note bottom of LOG
  **Nothing is lost.** A fact that leaves the
  screen, because sbx says it or because it is
  a how-to, stays in the run log.
end note

note bottom of WAVES
  **One wave per stream.** Each wave moves its
  own e2e anchors and specs in the same change,
  so the suite never reads a stale string.
end note
@enduml
